<%# The move list in PDN, as numbered pairs, with one move highlighted. The pairing and the
    notation come from Draughts::PDN, so the list and an exported .pdn file can never
    disagree. A whole jump sequence is one entry (24x15x8), because it is one move.

    Two locals, so that the match page and the replay page share this list: pairs is what
    move_pairs (from the engine's game) or move_pairs_from_rows (from the stored move rows)
    built, and highlight is the ply to mark. The match page highlights the latest move; the
    replay page highlights the ply it is showing.

    The moves controller scrolls the highlighted entry into the list's own scroll box, here and
    on every Turbo Stream replacement of this fragment. It holds no rule and no data; with
    JavaScript off the list is the same list and the reader scrolls it by hand. %>
<div id="<%= Match::MOVES_ID %>" class="moves" data-controller="moves">
  <h2 class="moves__heading">Moves</h2>
  <% if pairs.empty? %>
    <p class="moves__empty">No moves yet.</p>
  <% else %>
    <ol class="moves__list">
      <% pairs.each do |number, red, white| %>
        <li class="moves__pair">
          <span class="moves__number"><%= number %>.</span>
          <% if red.nil? %>
            <%# Only a game set up from a position can open with White's move; PDN writes the
                missing Red move as an ellipsis. %>
            <span class="moves__move moves__move--none">...</span>
          <% end %>
          <% [ red, white ].compact.each do |entry| %>
            <%# aria-current, not the colour alone: the highlight is the whole point of the
                replay page and a screen reader was told nothing about it (round-2
                accessibility audit, finding M1). The tag helper drops the attribute on every
                other entry rather than writing aria-current="". %>
            <%= tag.span entry.pdn,
                  class: class_names("moves__move",
                                     "moves__move--latest" => entry.ply == highlight),
                  aria: { current: ("true" if entry.ply == highlight) },
                  data: { ply: entry.ply } %>
          <% end %>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ol>
  <% end %>
</div>
